#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:1
msgid "Migrating ROS 2 packages that use Gazebo Classic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:3
msgid ""
"The Gazebo simulator has its roots in the Gazebo Classic project, but it has "
"a few significant differences that affect how a ROS 2 project uses the "
"simulator. One difference is that ROS 2 projects now use the [ros_gz]"
"(https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) package instead of [gazebo_ros_pkgs]"
"(https://github.com/ros-simulation/gazebo_ros_pkgs) as the source of launch "
"files and other useful utilities. Another major difference is that while "
"[gazebo_ros_pkgs](https://github.com/ros-simulation/gazebo_ros_pkgs) "
"provided a set of plugins that directly get loaded by Gazebo Classic and run "
"as part of the simulation to provide an interface between ROS and Gazebo "
"Classic, [ros_gz](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) is primarily used as "
"a bridge between ROS and gz-transport topics. Knowing these conceptual "
"differences is important in making the transition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:16
msgid ""
"**Note:** Since the name of the project has gone through two major changes, "
"we highly recommend you read the [history](https://gazebosim.org/about) of "
"the project to have a better understanding of the terminology used in this "
"tutorial and elsewhere. As a convention we refer to older versions of "
"Gazebo, those with release numbers like Gazebo 9 and Gazebo 11 as \"Gazebo "
"Classic.\" Newer versions of Gazebo, formerly called \"Ignition\", with "
"lettered releases names like Harmonic, are referred to as just \"Gazebo\" in "
"this document. This tutorial will show how to migrate an existing ROS 2 "
"package that uses the `gazebo_ros_pkgs` package to the new `ros_gz`. We will "
"use the [turtlebot3_simulations](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/) package as an example. The complete, migrated "
"version of `turtlebot3_simulations` covered in this tutorial, can be found "
"in [this fork](https://github.com/azeey/turtlebot3_simulations/tree/"
"new_gazebo)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:30
msgid ""
"We'll start by following the [PC Setup](https://emanual.robotis.com/docs/en/"
"platform/turtlebot3/quick-start/) guide to install the necessary "
"prerequisites for simulating Turtlebot3. This will install additional "
"packages, such as [Nav2](https://github.com/ros-planning/navigation2) and "
"[Cartographer](https://github.com/cartographer-project/cartographer), which "
"we will be using later on in this tutorial, so make sure to not skip this "
"step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:38
msgid ""
"The next step is to clone the `turtlebot3_simulation` package. We'll use the "
"`humble-devel` branch, which at the time of writing had a SHA of `d16cdbe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:41
msgid ""
"source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash\n"
"mkdir -p ~/turtlebot3_ws/src\n"
"cd ~/turtlebot3_ws/src\n"
"git clone -b humble-devel https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:48
msgid "Install dependencies using `rosdep`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:50
msgid ""
"sudo rosdep init # only needed if  using rosdep\n"
"rosdep install --from-paths . -i -y\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:55
msgid ""
"Finally, build the project and check that the Gazebo classic simulation "
"works. (See the [Gazebo Simulation guide](https://emanual.robotis.com/docs/"
"en/platform/turtlebot3/simulation/#gazebo-simulation))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:59
msgid ""
"cd ~/turtlebot3_ws\n"
"colcon build --symlink-install\n"
"source ~/turtlebot3_ws/install/setup.bash\n"
"\n"
"export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=waffle\n"
"ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo empty_world.launch.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:68
msgid ""
"Here's a screenshot of Turtlebot3 running in Gazebo Classic obtained by "
"launching `empty_world.launch.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:71
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of turtlebot 3 running in Gazebo Classic](images/"
"gz_ros2_migration/gazebo_classic_turtlebot3.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:71
msgid "Screenshot of turtlebot 3 running in Gazebo Classic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:73
msgid ""
"Once, we're sure that the Gazebo classic simulation is running properly, we "
"create a new branch in which we'll make the changes to migrate to the new "
"Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:77
msgid "git checkout -b new_gazebo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:81
msgid "The changes we need to make are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:83
msgid ""
"Modify `package.xml` and `CMakeLists.txt` files replacing `gazebo`, "
"`gazebo_ros_pkgs`, etc with packages from `ros_gz`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:85
msgid "Edit launch files that start Gazebo (e.g. `empty_world.launch.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:86
msgid "Update the world SDFormat file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:87
msgid "Edit launch files that spawn models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:88
msgid "Edit model SDFormat files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:89
msgid "Bridge ROS topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:91
msgid "Update package dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:93
msgid ""
"The turtlebot 3 package depends on `gazebo_ros_pkgs`, which is the package "
"that provides launch files, plugins, and other utilities for using Gazebo "
"classic with ROS 2. The equivalent for the new Gazebo is `ros_gz`, but "
"`ros_gz` is actually a meta-package that contains a few packages. It's okay "
"to replace `gazebo_ros_pkgs` with `ros_gz` here, but using just the subset "
"of packages needed for your project will reduce the number of dependencies. "
"For the `turtlebot3_simulation` package, we will only need `ros_gz_bridge`, "
"`ros_gz_image`, and `ros_gz_sim` for now. `ros_gz_bridge` and `ros_gz_image` "
"provide topic bridges between Gazebo and ROS while `ros_gz_sim` provides "
"launch files and other utilities that help with starting Gazebo and spawning "
"models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:104
msgid ""
"After making the change, lines 17-21 of `package.xml` will look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:106
msgid ""
"...\n"
"  <depend>geometry_msgs</depend>\n"
"  <depend>nav_msgs</depend>\n"
"  <depend>rclcpp</depend>\n"
"  <depend>ros_gz_bridge</depend>\n"
"  <depend>ros_gz_image</depend>\n"
"  <depend>ros_gz_sim</depend>\n"
"  <depend>sensor_msgs</depend>\n"
"  <depend>tf2</depend>\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:119
msgid ""
"You can find the [Gazebo Classic package XML file here](https://github.com/"
"ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/turtlebot3_gazebo/package.xml), and "
"the [updated Gazebo package XML file here](https://github.com/azeey/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/new_gazebo/turtlebot3_gazebo/package.xml)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:124
msgid ""
"After making the change, we'll need to install the new dependencies. The "
"following command will automatically install the necessary Gazebo version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:127
msgid "rosdep install --from-paths . -i -y\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:131
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes you are using Gazebo Fortress as it is the version of "
"Gazebo officially paired with ROS 2 Humble. While it is possible to use "
"newer versions of Gazebo with ROS 2 Humble, it requires extra work and is "
"not recommend for most users. See [Installing Gazebo with ROS]"
"(ros_installation) to learn more. If you intend to switch back and forth "
"between the new Gazebo and Gazebo Classic, it's best to use Gazebo Fortress "
"since the newer versions will automatically uninstall Gazebo Classic. With "
"that being said, the concepts covered by the tutorial should work with newer "
"versions of ROS 2 and Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:141
msgid "Launch the world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:143
msgid ""
"We now need to edit `turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/empty_world.launch.py` and "
"replace any use of `gazebo_ros_pkgs`. You can find the [Gazebo Classic empty "
"world launch file before editing here](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/empty_world.launch.py), and the [updated Gazebo "
"empty world launch file here](https://github.com/azeey/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/new_gazebo/turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/empty_world."
"launch.py). First replace the call to `get_package_share_directory` to find "
"`ros_gz_sim`. The code will change from:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:151
msgid "pkg_gazebo_ros = get_package_share_directory('gazebo_ros')\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:155
msgid "to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:157
msgid "ros_gz_sim = get_package_share_directory('ros_gz_sim')\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:161
msgid "Next, change `gzserver_cmd` to use `ros_gz_sim`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:163
msgid ""
"gzserver_cmd = IncludeLaunchDescription(\n"
"    PythonLaunchDescriptionSource(\n"
"        os.path.join(ros_gz_sim, 'launch', 'gz_sim.launch.py')\n"
"    ),\n"
"    launch_arguments={'gz_args': ['-r -s -v4 ', world], 'on_exit_shutdown': "
"'true'}.items()\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:172
msgid ""
"This uses the `gz_sim.launch.py` launch file from the `ros_gz_sim` package. "
"The launch file takes the `gz_args` argument which is a list of command line "
"flags that will be passed to `ign gazebo` (`gz sim` in Garden and later). `-"
"s` causes only the Gazebo server to run without the GUI client and `-r` "
"tells Gazebo to start running simulation immediately. Lastly, we are using "
"the `-v4` flag which sets the verbosity level of Gazebo's console output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:179
msgid ""
"**Note:** The list assigned to `gz_args` is concatenated into a string with "
"code equivalent to `''.join(gz_args)`, so it's important to keep whitespace "
"where necessary. Note the space after 4 in `'-v4 '`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:183
msgid ""
"The `world` argument will be substituted by `launch` before running Gazebo. "
"In this launch file, `world` is a python variable, so it is possible to use "
"python string formatting: `gz_args: f'-s -r -v4 {world}'`. But if we wanted "
"to use a `LaunchConfiguration` variable for `world`, we will need to use a "
"list so that `launch` will make the substitution for us."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:189
msgid ""
"The `on_exit_shutdown` argument ensures that if the Gazebo server exits for "
"any reason, the rest of the nodes in the launch file are shutdown"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:192
msgid ""
"The GUI client is launched in a similar way, but we change `gz_args` to `-g` "
"to run just the GUI client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:195
msgid ""
"gzclient_cmd = IncludeLaunchDescription(\n"
"    PythonLaunchDescriptionSource(\n"
"        os.path.join(ros_gz_sim, 'launch', 'gz_sim.launch.py')\n"
"    ),\n"
"    launch_arguments={'gz_args': '-g -v4 '}.items()\n"
")\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:205
msgid ""
"<!-- This env variable section might not be needed if\n"
"https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/pull/492 gets merged -->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:208
msgid ""
"Finally, we need to set the environment variable `GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH` so "
"Gazebo can know where to find models. See the [Finding resource](https://"
"gazebosim.org/api/sim/8/resources.html) document to learn more about this "
"environment variable. This was not needed for `gazebo_ros_pkgs` because it "
"used the `<export>` tag in `package.xml` to populate a similar environment "
"variable for Gazebo (`GAZEBO_MODEL_PATH`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:215
msgid "First, import `AppendEnvironmentVariable`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:217
msgid "from launch.actions import AppendEnvironmentVariable\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:221
msgid ""
"and create a `launch` action that appends the environment variable with the "
"location of the `models` directory in `turtlebot3_gazebo`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:224
msgid ""
"\n"
"set_env_vars_resources = AppendEnvironmentVariable(\n"
"        'GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH',\n"
"        os.path.join(get_package_share_directory('turtlebot3_gazebo'),\n"
"                     'models'))\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:233
msgid ""
"We'll then need to add the action to `ld`, the `LaunchDescription` variable "
"returned by `generate_launch_description`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:236
msgid "ld.add_action(set_env_vars_resources)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:240
msgid "<!-- end env variable section -->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:242
msgid ""
"We are now ready to test the launch file. Comment out `ld."
"add_action(spawn_turtlebot_cmd)` and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:245
msgid "ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo empty_world.launch.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:249
msgid ""
"**More than likely, this will fail** because Gazebo could not find models "
"referenced in the world SDFormat file. The next step is to fix that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:252
msgid ""
"**Note:** Due to a bug in the GUI client, there might be a lingering `ign "
"gazebo -g` or `gz sim -g` process after terminating the launch. You can kill "
"it using `pkill -f -9 'ign gazebo'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:256
msgid "Edit world SDFormat file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:258
msgid ""
"The file we will be editing is `turtlebot3_gazebo/worlds/empty_world.world`. "
"This file references the models `sun` and `ground_plane`. In Gazebo Classic, "
"these models were either shipped with the simulator or downloaded from the "
"gazebo [model repository](https://github.com/osrf/gazebo_models). The new "
"Gazebo does not ship these models, instead we can use models from Fuel or "
"add the models directly to the world file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:265
msgid ""
"To use fuel models, replace the `include` tags for `sun` and `ground_place` "
"with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:267
msgid ""
"<include>\n"
"  <uri>\n"
"    https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Ground Plane\n"
"  </uri>\n"
"</include>\n"
"\n"
"<include>\n"
"  <uri>\n"
"    https://fuel.gazebosim.org/1.0/OpenRobotics/models/Sun\n"
"  </uri>\n"
"</include>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:281
msgid ""
"For reference, you can find the [Gazebo Classic empty world here](https://"
"github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/turtlebot3_gazebo/worlds/"
"empty_world.world), and the [updated new Gazebo empty world here](https://"
"github.com/azeey/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/new_gazebo/turtlebot3_gazebo/"
"worlds/empty_world.world). Relaunching `empty_world.launch.py` should now "
"start the simulator successfully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:287
msgid "Spawn model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:289
msgid ""
"In this step, we will modify `turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/spawn_turtlebot3."
"launch.py`. Again, we need to change `gazebo_ros` to `ros_gz_sim`. We'll "
"also need to change `spawn_entity.py` to `create`, which is the node in "
"`ros_gz_sim` that provides model spawning functionality. From the argument "
"list, `-entity` needs to be replaced with `-name`. You can run `ros2 run "
"ros_gz_sim create --helpshort` to see more options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:297
msgid "The resulting `Node` should look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:299
msgid ""
"start_gazebo_ros_spawner_cmd = Node(\n"
"    package='ros_gz_sim',\n"
"    executable='create',\n"
"    arguments=[\n"
"        '-name', TURTLEBOT3_MODEL,\n"
"        '-file', urdf_path,\n"
"        '-x', x_pose,\n"
"        '-y', y_pose,\n"
"        '-z', '0.01'\n"
"    ],\n"
"    output='screen',\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:314
msgid ""
"If you uncomment `ld.add_action(spawn_turtlebot_cmd)` in `empty_world.launch."
"py` and run the launch file, you'll notice errors related to unrecognized "
"plugins. These are coming from the model SDFormat file, which we will modify "
"next."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:318
msgid "Modify the model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:320
msgid ""
"We will be using the `waffle` robot for this tutorial, so we'll edit the "
"file [`turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf`](https://github."
"com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/turtlebot3_gazebo/models/"
"turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf). The changes we need to make are mostly related "
"to plugins and their parameters. You can reference the Waffle [model SDF "
"file before editing here](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf), and [after editing "
"here](https://github.com/azeey/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/new_gazebo/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf). The following is a "
"list of all the plugins in the original model. For each plugin, we will "
"either remove the plugin if it's no longer necessary, or use the equivalent "
"plugin from the new Gazebo. You can use the Feature comparison page "
"([Fortress](https://gazebosim.org/docs/fortress/comparison), [Harmonic]"
"(https://gazebosim.org/docs/harmonic/comparison)) to find out of a Gazebo "
"Classic feature (e.g. a Sensor type) is available in Gazebo. If an "
"equivalent plugin is used, we will update the SDF parameters of the plugin "
"to match the parameters of the new plugin. See the list of systems "
"([Fortress](https://gazebosim.org/api/gazebo/6/"
"namespaceignition_1_1gazebo_1_1systems.html), [Harmonic](https://gazebosim."
"org/api/sim/8/namespacegz_1_1sim_1_1systems.html)) to find equivalent "
"plugins and their parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:339
msgid "libgazebo_ros_imu_sensor.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:341
msgid ""
"[Plugin in the original model](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf#L89-L94)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:343
msgid ""
"This plugin can be removed since there is a generic IMU plugin that handles "
"all IMU sensors. We will add this to the world later. We will set the "
"`<topic>` tag inside `<sensor>` to a short topic name to make it easier when "
"creating a ROS bridge later. The entire `<sensor>` tag should now look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:348
msgid ""
"<link name=\"imu_link\">\n"
"  <sensor name=\"tb3_imu\" type=\"imu\">\n"
"    <always_on>true</always_on>\n"
"    <update_rate>200</update_rate>\n"
"    <topic>imu</topic>\n"
"    <imu>\n"
"      ... <!-- all the content of <imu> -->\n"
"    </imu>\n"
"  </sensor>\n"
"</link>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:361
msgid "libgazebo_ros_ray_sensor.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:363
msgid ""
"[Plugin in the original model](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations//blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf#L157-L164)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:365
msgid ""
"Similar to the IMU, we will use a generic plugin loaded into the world for "
"handling all rendering sensors, which includes Lidar sensors. Currently the "
"`ray` sensor type, which meant to use the physics engine for generating the "
"sensor data, is not supported in the new Gazebo, we will need to update it "
"to `gpu_lidar`. We'll also need to change the `<ray>` tag inside `<sensor>` "
"to `<lidar>`. The `frame_name` parameter of the plugin will be handled by "
"setting the `gz_frame_id` parameter in `<sensor>`. Lastly, we'll set the "
"`<topic>` parameter similar to the IMU sensor. The final `<sensor>` tag for "
"the Lidar should look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:375
msgid ""
"<sensor name=\"hls_lfcd_lds\" type=\"gpu_lidar\">\n"
"  <always_on>true</always_on>\n"
"  <visualize>true</visualize>\n"
"  <pose>-0.064 0 0.121 0 0 0</pose>\n"
"  <update_rate>5</update_rate>\n"
"  <topic>scan</topic>\n"
"  <gz_frame_id>base_scan</gz_frame_id>\n"
"  <lidar>\n"
"    ... <!-- same content as <ray> in the original -->\n"
"  </lidar>\n"
"</sensor>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:389
msgid "libgazebo_ros_camera.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:391
msgid ""
"[Plugin in the original model](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations//blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf#L393-L402)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:393
msgid ""
"The Camera sensor will also use a generic plugin that handles all rendering "
"sensors loaded into the world. In the SDF file, we will set the `<topic>` "
"tag inside `<sensor>`, and the `<camera_info_topic>` inside `<camera>`, both "
"of which will be used in the ROS bridge later. We will also set the "
"`<gz_frame_id>` since the default frame id used by the generic plugin in the "
"new Gazebo is different from the default used by `libgazebo_ros_camera` in "
"Gazebo Classic. The final `<sensor>` tag should look like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:401
msgid ""
"<sensor name=\"camera\" type=\"camera\">\n"
"  <always_on>true</always_on>\n"
"  <visualize>true</visualize>\n"
"  <update_rate>30</update_rate>\n"
"  <topic>camera/image_raw</topic>\n"
"  <gz_frame_id>camera_rgb_frame</gz_frame_id>\n"
"  <camera name=\"intel_realsense_r200\">\n"
"    <camera_info_topic>camera/camera_info</camera_info_topic>\n"
"    ... <!-- all the content of <camera> from the original -->\n"
"  </camera>\n"
"</sensor>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:415
msgid "libgazebo_ros_diff_drive.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:417
msgid ""
"[Plugin in the original model](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations//blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf#L476-L507)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:419
msgid ""
"Since this is a model specific plugin, we will replace it with the "
"`DiffDrive` plugin. We will match the parameters of "
"`libgazebo_ros_diff_drive` as much as possible, but exact match may not be "
"possible. For example, the original plugin has a `max_wheel_acceleration`, "
"but `gz-sim-diff-drive-system` has `max_linear_acceleration` instead, which "
"are not equivalent; the latter is a limit on the whole vehicle's linear "
"acceleration. We can approximate the value by multiplying the wheel "
"acceleration limit by the radius of the wheel. Refer to the [DiffDrive class "
"reference](https://gazebosim.org/api/gazebo/6/"
"classignition_1_1gazebo_1_1systems_1_1DiffDrive.html) for details on each "
"parameter. Here's the full `<plugin>` tag with comments describing the "
"mapping from the original plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:431
msgid ""
"<plugin filename=\"gz-sim-diff-drive-system\" name=\"gz::sim::systems::"
"DiffDrive\">\n"
"  <!-- Remove <ros> tag. -->\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- wheels -->\n"
"  <left_joint>wheel_left_joint</left_joint>\n"
"  <right_joint>wheel_right_joint</right_joint>\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- kinematics -->\n"
"  <wheel_separation>0.287</wheel_separation>\n"
"  <wheel_radius>0.033</wheel_radius> <!-- computed from <wheel_diameter> in "
"the original plugin-->\n"
"\n"
"  <!-- limits -->\n"
"  <max_linear_acceleration>0.033</max_linear_acceleration> <!-- computed "
"from <max_linear_acceleration> in the original plugin-->\n"
"\n"
"  <topic>cmd_vel</topic> <!-- from <commant_topic> -->\n"
"\n"
"  <odom_topic>odom</odom_topic> <!-- from <odometry_topic> -->\n"
"  <frame_id>odom</frame_id> <!-- from <odometry_frame> -->\n"
"  <child_frame_id>base_footprint</child_frame_id> <!-- from "
"<robot_base_frame> -->\n"
"  <odom_publisher_frequency>30</odom_publisher_frequency> <!-- from "
"<update_rate>-->\n"
"\n"
"  <tf_topic>/tf</tf_topic> <!-- Short topic name for tf output -->\n"
"\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:459
msgid ""
"The `<wheel_torque>` parameter can be realized by setting effort limits on "
"each `<joint>`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:462
msgid ""
"<joint name=\"wheel_right_joint\" type=\"revolute\">\n"
"  <parent>base_link</parent>\n"
"  <child>wheel_right_link</child>\n"
"  <pose>0.0 -0.144 0.023 -1.57 0 0</pose>\n"
"  <axis>\n"
"    <xyz>0 0 1</xyz>\n"
"    <limit>\n"
"      <effort>20</effort> <!-- from <wheel_torque> in "
"libgazebo_ros_diff_drive.so.-->\n"
"    </limit>\n"
"  </axis>\n"
"</joint>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:476
msgid "libgazebo_ros_joint_state_publisher.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:478
msgid ""
"[Plugin in the original model](https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/"
"turtlebot3_simulations//blob/d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/"
"turtlebot3_gazebo/models/turtlebot3_waffle/model.sdf#L509-L517)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:480
msgid ""
"We will replace this plugin as well with [`JointStatePublisher`](https://"
"gazebosim.org/api/gazebo/6/"
"classignition_1_1gazebo_1_1systems_1_1JointStatePublisher.html). The "
"parameters are mostly similar, however, the `<update_rate>` parameter is not "
"supported. Here's the full `<plugin>` tag with comments describing the "
"mapping from the original plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:486
msgid ""
"<plugin filename=\"gz-sim-joint-state-publisher-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::JointStatePublisher\">\n"
"  <topic>joint_states</topic> <!--from <ros><remapping> -->\n"
"  <joint_name>wheel_left_joint</joint_name>\n"
"  <joint_name>wheel_right_joint</joint_name>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:495
msgid "World plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:497
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier, sensors are handled by generic world level plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:499
msgid ""
"<div class=\"warning\">\n"
"  By default, if there are no world plugins specified, Gazebo adds the "
"Physics,\n"
"  SceneBroadcaster, and UserCommands plugins. However, if we specify any\n"
"  plugins at all, Gazebo will assume we want to override the defaults, so "
"will not\n"
"  add any default plugins.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:506
msgid ""
"Therefore, we have to add the additional plugins for IMU and Lidar sensors "
"as well as the ones that would have been added by default. We will once "
"again edit `turtlebot3_gazebo/worlds/empty_world.world` add the following "
"right after `<world name=\"default\">`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:511
msgid ""
"<plugin\n"
"  filename=\"gz-sim-physics-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::Physics\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"<plugin\n"
"  filename=\"gz-sim-user-commands-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::UserCommands\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"<plugin\n"
"  filename=\"gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"<plugin\n"
"  filename=\"gz-sim-sensors-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::Sensors\">\n"
"  <render_engine>ogre2</render_engine>\n"
"</plugin>\n"
"<plugin\n"
"  filename=\"gz-sim-imu-system\"\n"
"  name=\"gz::sim::systems::Imu\">\n"
"</plugin>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:535
msgid "Bridge ROS topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:537
msgid ""
"In Gazebo Classic, communication with ROS is enabled by plugins in "
"`gazebo_ros_pkgs` that directly interface with the simulator. In contrast, "
"in the new Gazebo, communication with ROS is mainly done through topic "
"bridges provided by `ros_gz`. The bridge node is a generic node that bridges "
"topics between `gz-transport` and ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:543
msgid ""
"To create the bridge, we'll use a `yaml` file that contains the topic names "
"and their mappings. We'll add a new directory `params` in "
"`turtlebot3_gazebo` and create `turtlebot3_waffle_bridge.yaml` with the "
"following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:547
msgid ""
"# gz topic published by the simulator core\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"clock\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"clock\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"rosgraph_msgs/msg/Clock\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.Clock\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by JointState plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"joint_states\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"joint_states\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"sensor_msgs/msg/JointState\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.Model\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by DiffDrive plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"odom\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"odom\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.Odometry\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by DiffDrive plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"tf\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"tf\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"tf2_msgs/msg/TFMessage\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.Pose_V\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic subscribed to by DiffDrive plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"cmd_vel\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"cmd_vel\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"geometry_msgs/msg/Twist\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.Twist\"\n"
"  direction: ROS_TO_GZ\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by IMU plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"imu\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"imu\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"sensor_msgs/msg/Imu\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.IMU\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by Sensors plugin\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"scan\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"scan\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"sensor_msgs/msg/LaserScan\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.LaserScan\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
"\n"
"# gz topic published by Sensors plugin (Camera)\n"
"- ros_topic_name: \"camera/camera_info\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"camera/camera_info\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"sensor_msgs/msg/CameraInfo\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.CameraInfo\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:605
msgid ""
"[The completed yaml file can be found here.](https://github.com/azeey/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/blob/new_gazebo/turtlebot3_gazebo/params/"
"turtlebot3_waffle_bridge.yaml) Each entry in the yaml file has a ROS topic "
"name, a Gazebo topic name, a ROS data/message type, and a direction which "
"indicates which way messages flow. We will need to update the [`CMakeLists."
"txt`](https://github.com/azeey/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"ccb2385fd478e79c898d290d80fa41f35b1bbb83/turtlebot3_gazebo/CMakeLists."
"txt#L72) file to install the new `params` directory we created. The CMake "
"`install` command should look like"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:613
msgid ""
"install(DIRECTORY launch models params rviz urdf worlds\n"
"  DESTINATION share/${PROJECT_NAME}/\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:619
msgid ""
"Finally, we will edit [`turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py`]"
"(https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations//blob/"
"d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/"
"spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py), to create the bridge node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:623
msgid ""
"bridge_params = os.path.join(\n"
"    get_package_share_directory('turtlebot3_gazebo'),\n"
"    'params',\n"
"    'turtlebot3_waffle_bridge.yaml'\n"
")\n"
"\n"
"start_gazebo_ros_bridge_cmd = Node(\n"
"    package='ros_gz_bridge',\n"
"    executable='parameter_bridge',\n"
"    arguments=[\n"
"        '--ros-args',\n"
"        '-p',\n"
"        f'config_file:={bridge_params}',\n"
"    ],\n"
"    output='screen',\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:642
msgid ""
"You might have noticed that in the bridge parameters, we did not include the "
"`camera/image_raw` topic. While it is possible to bridge the image topic in "
"a similar manner as all the other topics, we will make use of a specialized "
"bridge node, [`ros_gz_image`](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/tree/ros2/"
"ros_gz_image), which provides a much more efficient bridge for image topics. "
"We'll add the following snippet to `turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/"
"spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:650
msgid ""
"start_gazebo_ros_image_bridge_cmd = Node(\n"
"    package='ros_gz_image',\n"
"    executable='image_bridge',\n"
"    arguments=['/camera/image_raw'],\n"
"    output='screen',\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:659
msgid ""
"Finally, we will add all the new actions to the list of `LaunchDescription`s "
"returned by the `generate_launch_description` function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:662
msgid ""
"# ...\n"
"\n"
"# Add the action to `ld` toward the end of the file\n"
"\n"
"ld.add_action(start_gazebo_ros_bridge_cmd)\n"
"ld.add_action(start_gazebo_ros_image_bridge_cmd)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:672
msgid ""
"You can find the [Gazebo Classic `spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py` file here]"
"(https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"d16cdbe7ecd601ccad48f87f77b6d89079ec5ac1/turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/"
"spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py), and the [updated Gazebo `spawn_turtlebot3."
"launch.py` file here](https://github.com/azeey/turtlebot3_simulations/blob/"
"new_gazebo/turtlebot3_gazebo/launch/spawn_turtlebot3.launch.py)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:677
msgid ""
"We are now ready to launch the empty world which spawns the waffle robot and "
"sets up the bridge so that we can communicate with it from ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:680
msgid ""
"export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=waffle\n"
"ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo empty_world.launch.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:685
msgid ""
"Here's a screenshot of Turtlebot3 running in Gazebo obtained by launching "
"`empty_world.launch.py`. The Lidar visualization is enabled by adding the "
"\"Visualize Lidar\" GUI plugin (see [tutorial](https://gazebosim.org/docs/"
"fortress/gui) on how to add GUI plugins)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:690
msgid ""
"![Screenshot of turtlebot 3 running in Gazebo](images/gz_ros2_migration/"
"gazebo_turtlebot3.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:690
msgid "Screenshot of turtlebot 3 running in Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:692
msgid ""
"It is also now possible to do the [SLAM](https://emanual.robotis.com/docs/en/"
"platform/turtlebot3/slam_simulation/) and [Navigation](https://emanual."
"robotis.com/docs/en/platform/turtlebot3/nav_simulation/) tutorials from the "
"Turtlebot3 manual (make sure to select the Humble tab). However, it requires "
"updating `turtlebot3_world.world` and `turtlebot3_world.launch.py` files "
"according what we've discussed in this tutorial. For reference, those files "
"have also been migrated in [this fork](https://github.com/azeey/"
"turtlebot3_simulations/tree/new_gazebo)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:702
msgid "Migrating other files in turtlebot3_gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../migrating_gazebo_classic_ros2_packages.md:704
msgid ""
"This tutorial does not cover all aspects of migrating models and launch "
"files from Gazebo classic. Please see the [Gazebo Classic Migration]"
"(gazebo_classic_migration) document for more resources that help with "
"migrating other aspects, such as Gazebo Classic plugins, materials and "
"textures."
msgstr ""
